# Build context control.
#
# Without these, `docker build -f Dockerfile .` from the repo root ships
# ~144 MB of the vendored OpenCode tree to the daemon on every build, and
# the OpenCode image is built from its own context instead (see
# Dockerfile.opencode, referenced by docker-compose.yml with
# context: ./packages/opencode-src).

node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
.svelte-kit/
**/.svelte-kit/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/

*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
coverage/
test-results/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Organism runtime state — never bake a previous run's learned state
# into the image. The compose volume owns this at runtime.
packages/metamorfus-src/data/
packages/metamorfus-src/.battery-results.json
packages/metamorfus-src/.run-battery-output.txt
.tmp-context-*.json

# Documentation and local reports
docs/
*.md
!README.md